\cf2 Johnny supposed it was a slow day for cremations.\
Discretion being the better part of car insurance, Johnny parked four spaces away, but still managed to squeal the tyres into the gutter. He got out of the car as calmly as he could, and smoothed his bald head back as he approached the van. \
\'93Praise the Dawkins!\'94 one Elvis greeted.\
\'93And the One after the One!\'94 the one Elvine in the trio hailed.\
\'93Praise the Holy Momma,\'94 the last Elvi intoned.\
\'93Yes,\'94 Johnny answered, somewhat less enthusiastically. \'93The Holy Momma.\'94 He felt his heart shrink. He should have been overjoyed at having Sarah assist his lifelong work, but he felt only a constant hum of longing at having her so close and yet so\'85 pregnant.\
The Elvine slid the van\'92s side door back.\
Johnny stepped closer. He wasn\'92t sure what he should be looking at inside the van; all he saw was three guitar cases. \'93You have the discs for the Holy Momma?\'94\
The Elvine slapped open the catches of the nearest guitar case and tried to throw the lid back. It refused to budge. The Elvine chuckled. \'93I always miss one,\'94 she said as she flipped the final catch and opened the case.\
Johnny stifled a gasp, and almost choked instead, as the content of the case shimmered with gentle rainbow light.\
\'93How many does the Holy Momma want?\'94 the Elvine asked as she plucked three from seemingly dozens in the case. \'93Three, wasn\'92t it?\'94\
Johnny stammered.\
The Elvine made to toss one to him. \'93Here, catch!\'94\
\'93No! Stop!\'94\
\'93You don\'92t want them?\'94\
\'93Just hand them to me.\'94 Johnny's voice climbed to frequencies only dogs and stressed physicists could hear. \'93Carefully.\'94\
The Elvine shrugged and held them out for Johnny to take. \'93Compliments of the High Elvis.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Johnny accepted the discs and tried to breathe. \'93Do you know what happens if these discs resonate? We could create a temporal paradox in which we\'92d have to explain to ourselves why we're idiots!\'94\
\'93I don\'92t expect you ever have to explain why you\'92re an idiot.\'94 The Elvine said flatly. \'93Sir.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Johnny took a moment after a moment to parse that.\
\'93Please tell the Holy Momma, the High Elvis says he looks forward to the vigil,\'94 the Elvine said. \
\'93Vigil? Where?\'94\
\'93At the residence of the Holy Momma. For the birth of the Dawkins. Oh. Have you not been invited?\'94\
\'93What? Of course\'85 I have. It\'92s\'85 just that\'85 I understood it was confidential.\'94\
\'93I dunno about that,\'94 an Elvis said. \'93Reckon everyone in the Ghetto will be driving up for the birth.\'94\
\'93Yes, I guess they will.\'94 Johnny\'92s mind raced. \'93Does Mrs Shakti know of this?\'94\
The Elvi shrugged. \'93I guess. The Sages didn\'92t say.\'94\
\'93Okay. Pleasure doing business.\'94 The Elvine shut the guitar case lid and fastened the clasps.\
\'93Please,\'94 Johnny implored. \'93Store the rest of those\'85 somewhere stable. Possibly in another dimension.\'94\
\'93No need to worry, sir. We had a few accidents with melting rhinestones at first, but we\'92ve left very few craters, and now we\'92re pretty confident how to deploy them.\'94\
\'93Deploy them?\'94 Johnny was mortified. \'93But\'85 you need experts to\'85 experts like me. You don\'92t know what you\'92re doing!\'94\
